                <td bgcolor="#f0f0f0" width="20%" valign="top"><b>Recommendation:</b></td>
                <td id="customfield_18605-7672731-value" class="value" bgcolor="#ffffff" width="80%">      This hazard is reported by SecArch and the related service ticket is <a href="https://jira.oci.oraclecorp.com/browse/ODBX-9563" title="Administrative APIs are accessible over HTTP, leading to the transmission of sensitive data in plaintext, which can be intercepted or manipulated through man-in-the-middle (MITM) attacks" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="ODBX-9563"><strike>ODBX-9563</strike></a> (also reported by SecArch), due date is 12/30/2025 and a security exception has also been filed, approved and expires 30/Jan/2026 (SDR-31649).<br/>
<br/>
Service: Admin API / SecArch<br/>
Contact: <a href='mailto:prasanna.shetty@oracle.com'>prasanna.shetty@oracle.com</a> / <a href='mailto:shawn.jackson@oracle.com'>shawn.jackson@oracle.com</a><br/>
Recommendation: <a href="https://confluence.oraclecorp.com/confluence/display/OCIOSD/OSD+-+Forge-+Admin+Api">https://confluence.oraclecorp.com/confluence/display/OCIOSD/OSD+-+Forge-+Admin+Api</a>  - All admin APIs must require HTTPS with valid certificates and strong cipher suites (using project Forge).
  </td>
