    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
            &nbsp;<font color="#ffffff"><b>Description</b></font>&nbsp;
        </td>
        <td>&nbsp;</td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p>Administrative APIs are accessible over HTTP, leading to the transmission of sensitive data in plaintext, which can be intercepted or manipulated through man-in-the-middle (MITM) attacks - High. Description: Administrative APIs are accessible over HTTP instead of HTTPS. This exposes the system to interception, tampering, and impersonation via network-based attacks. Impact: Interception of sensitive data, MITM attacks, System Compromise - Reconfigure services, exfiltrate data, or delete records. This could lead to operational disruption and data breach.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <br/>

    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
            &nbsp;<font color="#ffffff"><b>Comments</b></font>&nbsp;
        </td>
        <td>&nbsp;</td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="grid" style="margin: 0;">
                <tr id="comment-header-18216145"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                        <a class="user-hover" rel="veganap" id="word_commented_veganap" href="https://jira.oci.oraclecorp.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=veganap">Venkat Ganapathy</a>
                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">11/Feb/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-18216145"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>This hazard can be resolved as all the related referenced ticket has been already resolved and I confirmed with the service team.</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-17912090"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                        <a class="user-hover" rel="veganap" id="word_commented_veganap" href="https://jira.oci.oraclecorp.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=veganap">Venkat Ganapathy</a>
                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">06/Jan/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-17912090"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://jira.oci.oraclecorp.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=mbarela" class="user-hover" rel="mbarela">Michael Barela</a> I confirmed with "Alexandru Munteanu" that <a href="https://jira.oci.oraclecorp.com/browse/ODBX-9563" title="Administrative APIs are accessible over HTTP, leading to the transmission of sensitive data in plaintext, which can be intercepted or manipulated through man-in-the-middle (MITM) attacks" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="ODBX-9563"><del>ODBX-9563</del></a> can be resolved which should technically resolved this hazard.</p>

<p>But if you look at  the security exception it was filed only for "Oasis Control Pane" service team but the impact could be widespread according to the Security Architecture team who initially filed this hazard. I am not sure how you would like to handle this ticket.</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-16884986"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                        <a class="user-hover" rel="veganap" id="word_commented_veganap" href="https://jira.oci.oraclecorp.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=veganap">Venkat Ganapathy</a>
                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">19/Aug/25</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-16884986"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>To find the latest status on this ticket please see latest comments from this related hazard: <a href="https://jira.oci.oraclecorp.com/browse/HAZARDLOG-66" title="Weak TCP auth model allows unauthorized access to admin interface." class="issue-link" data-issue-key="HAZARDLOG-66">HAZARDLOG-66</a></p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-16807801"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                        <a class="user-hover" rel="veganap" id="word_commented_veganap" href="https://jira.oci.oraclecorp.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=veganap">Venkat Ganapathy</a>
                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">09/Aug/25</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-16807801"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <ul>
	<li>Both these hazards should get fixed if the health check API port only performs health checks and not allow admin functions. </li>
	<li>Admin is using HTTP because it's exposed to the load balancer</li>
	<li>Have different port for health check API and admin API</li>
</ul>

        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-16797734"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                        <a class="user-hover" rel="veganap" id="word_commented_veganap" href="https://jira.oci.oraclecorp.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=veganap">Venkat Ganapathy</a>
                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">07/Aug/25</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-16797734"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>I have reached out to the reporter to ask for some clarifications.</p>
        </td></tr>
            </table>
